\b Printo Agent\b0\par
Internal software. Installed and supported by your own IT department; there is no third-party licence to accept.\par
\par
\b What this installs\b0\par
A Windows service, \i PrintoAgent\i0 , which runs as LocalSystem and starts with the machine.\par
A printer called \i Printo\i0 . Anything printed to it is examined page by page and sent on to this machine's real printers - carrier labels to the thermal printer, everything else to A4.\par
A tray application and two Start Menu entries, \i Printo\i0  and \i Printo Settings\i0 .\par
\par
\b What it does with documents\b0\par
Documents are rendered, measured and printed on this workstation. They are not uploaded. When the agent is connected to a Printo server, what crosses the network is measurements and job records - page sizes, rule outcomes, which printer a page reached - and, only when an operator was asked to resolve a page, a thumbnail of the pages in question.\par
\par
A copy of each document is kept in \i C:\\ProgramData\\Printo\\agent\i0  until it has printed, and for as long afterwards as the retention policy your administrator has set.\par
\par
\b Before it can print\b0\par
This machine's printers have to be mapped to roles once, in \i Printo Settings\i0 . Until that is done the agent accepts documents and holds them.\par
